    "peregrine": -5,
    "notes": "Printed values from p. 115 'A ready Table whereby to examine the Fortitudes and Debilities of the Planets': Essential Dignities - in his own house or mutual reception by house 5; in his exaltation or reception by exaltation 4; own triplicity 3; own term 2; decanate or face 1. Debilities - in his detriment 5; in his fall 4; peregrine 5. The table lists debilities in a separate 'Debilities' column as unsigned numbers; the minus signs here express that they count against the planet. Pp. 101-103 state the same dignity values in prose (house 'five dignities', exaltation 'four', triplicity 'three', terms 'two', face 'one'). The 1647 Wellcome copy also has a contemporary handwritten row under the p. 104 table reading 5,4,3,2,1 under the dignity columns and 5,4 under Detriment/Fall; this is a reader's annotation, not print.",
    "page": "115 (also 101-103)"
  },
  "problems": [
    "Gemini exaltation is printed as the Dragon's Head (North Node) at 3 Gemini, and Sagittarius exaltation as the Dragon's Tail (South Node) at 3 Sagittarius; correspondingly the Fall column shows the Dragon's Tail in Gemini and the Dragon's Head in Sagittarius. Recorded as printed ('North Node'/'South Node'), not as a planet; consumers wanting planets only should treat these as no planetary exaltation/fall.",
    "Exaltation cell is blank for Leo, Scorpio and Aquarius; Fall cell is blank for Taurus, Leo and Aquarius. Recorded as null. (Scorpio does have a printed fall, the Moon.)",
    "Cancer and Leo have both 'N' and 'D' in the day/night column (the luminaries have one house each); recorded as 'N D'.",
    "Triplicity: Lilly's table gives only day and night rulers (no participating ruler). Water signs show Mars for both day and night; the text on p. 105 says Mars 'according to Ptolomy and Naibod, ruleth onely that Triplicity both day and night'.",
    "Taurus 4th term end degree '26' is overwritten by hand in ink in the Wellcome copy (printed digit partly obscured); reading 26 is consistent with the sequence (22 < 26 < 30).",
    "The OCR text (djvu.txt) of the table is unusable (glyphs lost); all values were read visually from the page image of leaf n137, zoomed. The 1659 second edition was not consulted.",
    "skyscript.co.uk/deginf.html (Houlding's Degree Influences page, a secondary source) was fetched only through a summarising tool and its summary was unreliable (e.g. reported missing exaltations), so it was not used for any value.",
    "All sanity checks passed: 5 terms per sign, term end degrees strictly increasing and ending at 30, faces follow the Chaldean order cycling from Mars at 0 Aries."
  ]
